From 63acc9603eca724b7746578a271b5fe17fab609a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:47:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] nfs: optionally report file system size based on a space
 reservation

Motivation:
The NFS door reports a fixed total size of 1 EiB and the space used by
all files in the namespace. As a result, tools like df show a
meaningless size and free space, which makes them useless for users and
for monitoring.

Modification:
Add the nfs.fs-stat.space-token property. If set, DCacheAwareJdbcFs
looks up the space reservation through SpaceManager (using the existing
ReservationCaches space lookup cache) and reports the reservation size
as total space and the space no longer available in the reservation
(used and allocated) as used space. File counts are still taken from the
namespace. If the reservation can't be looked up, the namespace
statistics are reported as before.

The property is empty by default, in which case the behaviour is
unchanged and SpaceManager isn't contacted.

Result:
Sites can configure the NFS door so that df shows the size and free
space of a space reservation.

Fixes: #8275
Target: master
Require-book: yes
Require-notes: yes
Signed-off-by: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
