+## Reporting file system size
+
+By default, the NFS door reports a fixed total size of 1 EiB and the space used by all files in the
+namespace, which makes the output of tools like `df` of little use. Alternatively, the door can report
+the size and usage of a space reservation:
+
+```ini
+nfs.fs-stat.space-token = 1234
+```
+
+With this configuration the total size is the size of the space reservation, and the free space is
+the space that is still available in it, i.e., neither used nor allocated. The number of files is
+still taken from the namespace. If the space reservation can't be looked up, the door reports the
+default values.
+
+As the NFS protocol has no notion of per-directory size, a single space reservation is used for all
+exports of a door. The values are cached by the door for `nfs.fs-stat-cache.time`, which may need to
+be lowered for clients to see changes in a timely manner.
+
